// @test: an un-annotated closure parameter with no contextual signature is refused
// @description: #385 -- inference fills a parameter only when the enclosing context
//   supplies a matching fn(...) signature. An untyped binding supplies none, so the
//   closure is refused with a diagnostic rather than silently accepted (and the call is
//   never silently dropped).
// @category: lambda, closure, generics, inference
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: Cannot determine type of object in member expression.

main()<Int> -> {
    g = |x| -> x * 2
    println("g=" + g(3).to_string())
    return 0
}
